    <!-- Guide -->
    <string name="guide_title">Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">How Stave works, in the order a first day goes.</string>
    <string name="guide_open_title">Open any sound</string>
    <string name="guide_open_body">Pick a file, share one from another app, or press Record. MP3, WAV, FLAC, M4A, OGG, Opus, AIFF, the sound of a video — if the phone has it, Stave reads it. Your original is never changed: the app works on its own copy.</string>
    <string name="guide_edit_title">Edit by selecting</string>
    <string name="guide_edit_body">Drag to move through the sound; hold a moment, then drag, to select. Pinch to zoom. The play-head is the fixed line in the middle; the sound moves under it. Every change can be undone, even after you close the app.</string>
    <string name="guide_repair_title">Clean up</string>
    <string name="guide_repair_body">Clean up voice takes out hiss and room noise. Repair finds clicks, clipped peaks and mains hum and mends them. Open the spectrogram and paint over a cough to take it out of the sound around it.</string>
    <string name="guide_voice_title">Edit the words</string>
    <string name="guide_voice_body">Transcribe a recording and the words appear under the waveform. Tap words to select that stretch of audio; delete them and the audio goes with them. Take out every um and uh in one tap.</string>
    <string name="guide_studio_title">Layer tracks</string>
    <string name="guide_studio_body">Add as many tracks as the phone can play. Record over them into lanes, set volume and pan automation (Duck under speech writes it for you), send to buses, freeze a heavy track, and bounce the mix. Takes are kept in lanes so nothing you record is lost.</string>
    <string name="guide_music_title">Pull a song apart</string>
    <string name="guide_music_body">Separate vocals, drums, bass and the rest on the phone, with no upload and no monthly count. Read the chords, slow a passage, loop it, mute the vocal and record your own over it.</string>
    <string name="guide_beats_title">Make a beat</string>
    <string name="guide_beats_body">Tap steps on the grid or play the pads while the loop runs and they are written in. Drums, synths or any SoundFont you add; swing, quantise, an arpeggiator; a song of patterns rendered to tracks; MIDI files in and out.</string>
    <string name="guide_finish_title">Finish to a target</string>
    <string name="guide_finish_body">Pick where the sound is going — podcast, streaming, broadcast — and Stave brings it to that loudness with a true-peak ceiling. Export to MP3, FLAC, WAV, Opus, AAC or ALAC with chapters and artwork.</string>
    <string name="guide_privacy_title">Nothing leaves the phone</string>
    <string name="guide_privacy_body">Stave has no internet permission. The neural models that clean voices and separate songs run on the device. There is no account, no upload, no watermark, no limit, no subscription, and the source code is public.</string>
    <string name="guide_outro">Stuck on something? Contact is one tap away from the Home screen.</string>

